From 441533711d91492815b710a79b1ec4acb5e19ca6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:25:45 +0200
Subject: ALSA: caiaq: Register card at the final step
Git-commit: 441533711d91492815b710a79b1ec4acb5e19ca6
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

caiaq driver calls snd_card_register() before creating the mixer
elements, which is rather confusing to user-space, as the devices have
been published before adding the control elements.

Swap the call order to make the card registration as the final step
(as written in the comment).

Fixes: 8e3cd08ed8e5 ("[ALSA] caiaq - add control API and more input features")
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261008192553.300025-6-tiwai@suse.de
Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/usb/caiaq/device.c |   10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/usb/caiaq/device.c
+++ b/sound/usb/caiaq/device.c
@@ -388,16 +388,16 @@ static int setup_card(struct snd_usb_cai
 	}
 #endif
 
-	/* finally, register the card and all its sub-instances */
-	ret = snd_card_register(cdev->chip.card);
+	ret = snd_usb_caiaq_control_init(cdev);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		dev_err(dev, "snd_card_register() returned %d\n", ret);
+		dev_err(dev, "Unable to set up control system (ret=%d)\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = snd_usb_caiaq_control_init(cdev);
+	/* finally, register the card and all its sub-instances */
+	ret = snd_card_register(cdev->chip.card);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		dev_err(dev, "Unable to set up control system (ret=%d)\n", ret);
+		dev_err(dev, "snd_card_register() returned %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
